// A sea's surface at a pixel turned by its ripples (see SeaMaps): small waves its cells are too coarse to move, summed
// as slopes onto its normal before it is lit, fading out with distance, where a pixel covers many of them; and that
// normal kept facing the camera.
namespace Stride.Water
{
    shader SeaRipples : IMaterialSurface, SeaMaps, NormalStream
    {
        override void Compute()
        {
            float2 at = streams.PositionWS.xz;
            float distance = length(streams.PositionWS.xyz - Eye.xyz);
            float2 slope = 0;
            // Calming towards the shore (where its shore map says how deep it is).
            float wind = WindAt(ShoreAt(at).y);
            [unroll]
            for (int i = 0; i < 16; i++)
            {
                float2 direction = Ripples[i].xy;
                float k = Ripples[i].z;
                // Faded out once it is under about two pixels far off.
                float fade = saturate(2.0f - distance * k * 0.004f);
                float phase = k * dot(direction, at) - sqrt(9.81f * k) * Time;
                slope += direction * k * Ripples[i].w * cos(phase) * fade;
            }
            slope *= wind;
            float3 normal = normalize(streams.normalWS - float3(slope.x, 0.0f, slope.y));

            // Seen from low down, the back of a steep crest would reflect the ground under the horizon (black, as the
            // sky has nothing there), and almost all of it at such an angle: turned just enough that what it reflects is
            // the sky at the horizon, as distant water does. Its back faces' normals (turned away) are turned back too.
            float3 view = normalize(Eye.xyz - streams.PositionWS.xyz);
            if (dot(normal, view) < 0.0f)
                normal = normalize(normal - view * (2.0f * dot(normal, view)));
            float3 reflected = reflect(-view, normal);
            if (reflected.y < 0.03f)
            {
                reflected = normalize(float3(reflected.x, 0.03f, reflected.z));
                normal = normalize(view + reflected);
            }
            streams.normalWS = normal;
        }
    };
}
